Copyright 2025 wmserver contributors — Apache-2.0

This service wraps several inpainting backends behind adapters. License terms
differ; verify against current upstream before deployment (especially commercial):

Permissive (safe):
- FastAPI, Uvicorn, Starlette   — MIT/BSD
- OpenCV (opencv-python-headless) — Apache-2.0
- Pillow                        — HPND (permissive)
- vidfill (sibling package)     — Apache-2.0

Model backends (optional extras):
- IOPaint                       — Apache-2.0 (wraps LaMa and others)
- LaMa `big-lama` weights       — verify weight license separately
- ProPainter (sczhou/ProPainter) — **S-Lab NON-COMMERCIAL license**. Fine for
  personal/research use; NOT permitted for commercial deployment. The classical
  `vidfill`-based video backend is the permissive, always-available alternative.

The default `auto` backend selection prefers the model and falls back to the
classical CPU backend, so no non-permissive component is required to run the
service.
